# Paradigm Practices

## Habits Compliance

Paradigm tracks behavioral habits — repeatable practices that improve code quality.

### When to Check Habits

| Trigger | When | Tool |
|---------|------|------|
| `preflight` | Before starting implementation | `paradigm_habits_check({ trigger: "preflight" })` |
| `postflight` | After completing implementation | `paradigm_habits_check({ trigger: "postflight" })` |
| `on-stop` | Before ending a session | `paradigm_habits_check({ trigger: "on-stop" })` |

### Key Habit Categories

| Category | Examples |
|----------|----------|
| Discovery | Call `paradigm_ripple` before modifying symbols |
| Security | Declare gates for new routes in portal.yaml |
| Documentation | Update .purpose files for modified components |
| Quality | Record lore for sessions modifying 3+ files |

Use `paradigm_practice_context` before modifying symbols to get habit-aware warnings.


## Lore Recording

Lore captures the project timeline — sessions, decisions, milestones, and incidents.

### When to Record Lore

| Type | When | Example |
|------|------|---------|
| `agent-session` | After modifying 3+ files | "Added JWT auth to /api/projects" |
| `decision` | After making architectural choices | "Chose Redis over Memcached for caching" |
| `milestone` | After completing a significant feature | "v2.0 migration complete" |
| `incident` | After resolving a production issue | "Fixed OOM in payment worker" |

### Recording

```
paradigm_lore_record({
  type: "agent-session",
  title: "Short description of work done",
  summary: "Detailed summary of changes...",
  symbols_touched: ["#component", "^gate"]
})
```

Use `paradigm_lore_timeline` at session start for project history orientation.


## llms.txt

This project provides an `llms.txt` file at the repository root — a plain-text summary
of the project optimized for LLM consumption. It includes symbols, key files, flows,
gates, and conventions.

Regenerate with: `paradigm sync-llms`
